  methodology: 'The calculator converts device power in watts to kilowatts (÷1000), multiplies by the hours run per day to get daily energy in kWh, then multiplies by your entered electricity rate ($/kWh) to return daily cost. Monthly (×30) and yearly (×365) figures extrapolate that daily cost, matching the kWh-based billing model every US and international utility uses.',
